SUMMARY:🌳🌿 EVENING HIGH PARK SUMMER WALK 🌿🌳
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n🌳
 🌿 EVENING HIGH PARK SUMMER WALK 🌿🌳\n\nToronto's Biggest Park\, Hi
 dden Trails & Great Company\nHigh Park is Toronto's largest and most belov
 ed park — and once you start exploring it\, it's easy to understand why.
 \n\nFrom winding trails and forested paths to Grenadier Pond\, beautiful g
 ardens\, historic landmarks\, and even a small zoo\, High Park offers a li
 ttle bit of everything. Despite being right in the middle of the city\, pa
 rts of the park feel surprisingly wild and peaceful.\n\nJoin us for a rela
 xed social walk as we explore some of the best parts of High Park together
 .\n\nThis is not a historical tour.\n\nIt's a social walk focused on fresh
  air\, exercise\, conversation\, and enjoying one of Toronto's most beauti
 ful green spaces.\n\n**👉 Don't forget to join our WhatsApp group – [(
  Click here to join)](http://[click%20here!](%20click%20here%20to%20join)/
 )**\n\n***\n\n🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll spend approximately 2 h
 ours exploring High Park's trails\, pathways\, and scenic areas.\n\nAlong 
 the way we'll:\n🌳 Walk through wooded trails\n🦆 Visit Grenadier Pond
 \n📸 Stop at some of the park's most beautiful spots\n😊 Take a short 
 break along the route\n🚶 Continue exploring before returning to the sub
 way station\nPlease note there are several hills and a large staircase on 
 this route.\nNothing extreme\, but there are hills and stairs that you wil
 l be able to climb and you should be comfortable walking for an extended p
 eriod.\n\nThis walk is suitable for most people with a moderate fitness le
 vel.\n\n***\n\n☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis event happens rain or
  shine.\nSummer weather can change quickly\, so please dress appropriately
  and be prepared for sun\, heat\, or light rain.\n\nThe only reason we wou
 ld cancel is for severe weather conditions.\nThis is a social walking grou
 p\, not a race.\n\nWe'll keep a comfortable pace while still moving steadi
 ly through the park.\n\n***\n\n🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 Meetup Location
 : High Park Sign (west side of Bloor Street and High Park Avenue)\n🫎 I'
 ll be wearing my Moose Hat\n⏰ Meetup Time: 6:30pm\nI will only wait 5 mi
 nutes.\nEarly is on time.\nOn time is late.\n\n🏁 End Point: Back at Hig
 h Park Subway Station\n\n***\n\n🎟️ Meetup Fee: $5 cash in person or e
 -transfer to\n📧 **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotm
 ail.com)**\nThis fee helps support the group and allows us to continue org
 anizing events like this. Thank you for supporting community! 💖\n\n***\
 n\n🎒 What to Bring\n💧 Water\n👟 Good walking shoes\n🥨 A snack\n
 🧴 Sunscreen\n🕶️ Sunglasses\n\n***\n\n🌈 Who Is This For?\nThis g
 roup is open to anyone who wants to be social and make friends — whether
  single or not.\n\nWe also host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Ar
 ts & culture outings\n🍽️ Restaurant gatherings\nThere's always someth
 ing happening.\n\n***\n\nREMEMBER: You're welcome to just show up on the d
 ay if you're unsure about your schedule.\nAnd as always\, sometimes plans 
 shift and events may need to be cancelled — please keep an eye on update
 s.\n\n***\n\n👤 Organizer: Mathew\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or 
 email\n📧 [torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesando
 utings@hotmail.com)\n\nCome for the trails.\nStay for the conversation.\n\
 nLeave feeling like you've escaped the city without ever leaving it. 🌳
 ✨
