SUMMARY:🌅🌊 SUMMER EVENING WALK OF THE TORONTO ISLANDS (9KM) 🌊🌅
DESCRIPTION:Toronto Movies & Social Group - Celebrating 14 Years!\n🌅
 🌊 SUMMER EVENING WALK OF THE TORONTO ISLANDS (9KM) 🌊🌅\n\nSunset V
 iews\, Island Paths & Toronto's Best Skyline\nThere is something magical a
 bout the Toronto Islands in the evening.\n\nAs the city begins to slow dow
 n\, the islands come alive with golden light\, cool lake breezes\, and som
 e of the most spectacular views in Toronto. It feels like you've escaped t
 he city without ever leaving it.\nJoin us for a relaxed summer evening wal
 k across the T\n\nToronto Islands as we explore Hanlan's Point\, Centre Is
 land\, and Ward's Island while enjoying beaches\, open green spaces\, char
 ming cottages\, and breathtaking skyline views.\n\nThe Toronto Islands hav
 e a fascinating history. Originally connected to the mainland as a long sa
 ndbar peninsula\, a powerful storm in 1858 permanently separated the land 
 from Toronto\, creating the islands we know today.\n\nOver the years they'
 ve been home to amusement parks\, summer cottages\, beaches\, and the uniq
 ue island community that still exists today on Ward's Island.\n\nThis is n
 ot a formal historical tour.\nIt's a social walk with beautiful scenery\, 
 fresh air\, and great conversation.\n\n📲 **Join Our WhatsApp Group:**[ 
 Click here to join](https://chat.whatsapp.com/DRFTkxRlHS4B3IL1lMleUd)\n\n*
 **\n\n🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll take the ferry together to Hanl
 an's Point and begin our walk across the islands.\n\nOur route will take u
 s through:\n🌊 Hanlan's Point\n🌳 Centre Island\n🏡 Ward's Island\n
 📸 Multiple skyline viewpoints\n🏖️ Beaches and waterfront paths\n\n
 We'll stop throughout the evening to enjoy the scenery\, take photos\, and
  soak in one of Toronto's most beautiful summer experiences.\nAs the sun b
 egins to set\, we'll enjoy some of the best views of the city skyline anyw
 here in Toronto.\n\nFeel free to bring a snack or something small to share
 .\nYou're welcome to leave at any time or stay and explore after the walk.
 \n\n***\n\n☀️ Weather & Expectations\n\nThis event will happen in typi
 cal summer weather conditions.\nThat means warm temperatures\, sunshine\, 
 clouds\, or light rain.\nThe islands are often cooler and breezier than do
 wntown Toronto\, especially later in the evening\, so bringing a light swe
 ater or jacket is recommended.\n\nThe only reason we would cancel is for s
 evere weather or thunderstorms.\n\nAlso — this is NOT a guided historica
 l tour. I'll share bits of history throughout the walk\, but the focus is 
 social connection and enjoying the islands together.\n\n***\n\n🧢 Meetup
  Details\n📍 Meetup Location: Inside the Jack Layton Ferry Terminal besi
 de the bathrooms\n🫎 I'll be wearing my Moose Hat\n⏰ Meetup Time: 6:30
  PM\n🚢 Ferry Departure: 6:45 PM (Hanlan's Point Ferry)\nPLEASE BE ON TI
 ME.\n🚢 Ferry Return: 9:45 PM\nOnce we're on the ferry\, it will be very
  difficult to catch up with the group.\n🎟️ Ferry Ticket: (Insert Curr
 ent Fare)\n\nYou must purchase your ticket before arriving.\n[CLICK HERE F
 OR TICKETS!](https://secure.toronto.ca/FerryTicketOnline/tickets2/index.js
 p)\n\n***\n\n🎟️ Meetup Fee: $5 cash in person or e-transfer to\n📧 
 [mathewmaclean@hotmail.com](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)\n\nThis fee 
 helps support the group and allows us to continue hosting events like this
 . Thank you for supporting community! 💖\n\n***\n\n🎒 What to Bring\n
 💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🥨 A snack\n🧥 Light sweat
 er or jacket\n🕶️ Sunglasses\n📸 Camera or phone for photos\n🌅 A 
 sense of adventure\n\n***\n\n🌈 Who Is This For?\nThis group is open to 
 anyone who wants to be social and make friends — whether single or not.\
 nWe also host:\n🎬 Movies\n🚶 Walks & hikes\n🎭 Arts & culture outin
 gs\n🍽️ Restaurant gatherings\nThere's always something happening.\n\n
 ***\n\nREMEMBER: You're welcome to just show up on the day if you're unsur
 e about your schedule.\nAnd as always\, sometimes plans shift and events m
 ay need to be cancelled — please keep an eye on updates.\n\n***\n\n👤 
 Organizer: Mathew\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email\n📧 [toron
 tomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com
 )\nCome for the sunset.\nStay for the skyline.\nLeave feeling like you spe
 nt the evening somewhere far away from the city — even though it was rig
 ht beside it. 🌅✨
